VCS_Context:1:1: [no-edits-on-described-commits] Command `jj edit @` targets a non-empty described commit.
  Rationale: Directly mutating an already-described commit rewrites reviewed history in place and risks tangling unrelated work into an existing change.
  Suggestion: Create a child change on top with `jj new @` and squash intentional fixes selectively via `jj squash`.


